  "notes": [
    "**Enfadarse** is the reflexive form of **enfadar** (to anger someone)",
    "Regular **-AR verb** with reflexive pronouns",
    "No spelling changes or stem changes",
    "Past participle: **enfadado** (regular)",
    "More common in Spain; in Latin America, **enojarse** is preferred",
    "Used with \"con\": *enfadarse con alguien* (to get angry with someone)",
    "Common usage:",
    "*Me enfadé con él* (I got angry with him)",
    "*No te enfades* (Don't get angry)",
    "*Se enfadó mucho* (He/She got very angry)",
    "Related adjective: **enfadado/a** (angry, mad) - *Estoy enfadado* (I'm angry)",
    "Related noun: **el enfado** (anger, annoyance)",
    "Synonym in Latin America: **enojarse**"
  ],
